1
00:00:01,066 --> 00:00:03,048
[Power and Division]
GROUND...

2
00:00:03,048 --> 00:00:05,280
FURY!!!!

3
00:00:11,047 --> 00:00:12,343
Are you awake? 

4
00:00:13,487 --> 00:00:14,444
How many fingers am I holding up?

5
00:00:14,444 --> 00:00:15,531
Two...

6
00:00:15,531 --> 00:00:16,731
It's a V!

7
00:00:16,731 --> 00:00:18,422
I'm so glad you're alright.

8
00:00:18,422 --> 00:00:19,678
What happened?

9
00:00:19,678 --> 00:00:22,446
We managed to get out of there thanks to Blaion and Wild Guardy.

10
00:00:22,446 --> 00:00:24,870
As for Solid Horn, he disappeared into the forest.

11
00:00:24,870 --> 00:00:28,731
Since he had just arrived on Earth, he probably didn't have enough energy to run wild much longer.

12
00:00:28,731 --> 00:00:29,916
Ah! Where's Blue Cop?!

13
00:00:29,916 --> 00:00:32,176
Don't worry. I have him.

14
00:00:32,939 --> 00:00:34,207
Here.

15
00:00:34,207 --> 00:00:36,146
Why do you... have his card?

16
00:00:36,146 --> 00:00:39,551
Rest assured. I didn't tame him with my Metal Breath.

17
00:00:39,551 --> 00:00:40,908
You better not have!!

18
00:00:42,335 --> 00:00:47,115
Since you were unconscious, I told her that it'd be better if she sealed him instead of you.

19
00:00:47,115 --> 00:00:48,189
What?!

20
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:51,768
- I didn't ask for your help!!
- Jun!

21
00:00:51,768 --> 00:00:54,918
You're going to trip! You shouldn't be running yet!

22
00:00:55,561 --> 00:00:58,487
Mega Ambler, where are you? I need your help.

23
00:00:59,003 --> 00:00:59,703
YAOUGH!!

24
00:00:59,703 --> 00:01:00,250
All done.

25
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:01,639
Ow... Are you sure that'll do it?

26
00:01:01,639 --> 00:01:06,153
Yes. Now that you've been vaccinated, the Beast Virus is as harmless as the common cold. Next!

27
00:01:06,506 --> 00:01:08,939
Me think maybe some other ti-! Ack!

28
00:01:08,939 --> 00:01:10,998
The mighty Black Crew never runs from pain!

29
00:01:10,998 --> 00:01:13,156
It doesn't even hurt, Buffalo Crush!

30
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:15,093
Now, stay... still!

31
00:01:15,394 --> 00:01:17,525
- OW OW OW OW!!
- Good job, lad!

32
00:01:17,525 --> 00:01:20,781
You're up next, Mr. Heavy Iron... uh, where did he go?

33
00:01:20,781 --> 00:01:23,537
Sheesh, what'd you do this time to end up like this?

34
00:01:23,537 --> 00:01:27,382
If he met that Solid Horn guy, it's only natural he'd end up like this.

35
00:01:27,382 --> 00:01:29,326
Summon me next time he shows up.

36
00:01:29,326 --> 00:01:31,076
Let me ask you something, Blue Cop.

37
00:01:31,076 --> 00:01:34,228
How did it feel when you first gained the beast power?

38
00:01:34,228 --> 00:01:36,804
It was a completely different kind of power than anything I’d experienced before.

39
00:01:36,804 --> 00:01:38,991
Not only was the pain indescribable,

40
00:01:38,991 --> 00:01:42,680
but I was also overwhelmed by the fear that I would no longer be able to contain that power.

41
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:45,628
The Star Guardian who knocked me to the ground was scared?

42
00:01:45,628 --> 00:01:47,677
I'm curious to see what that power is like...

43
00:01:47,677 --> 00:01:50,723
Watch your mouth! You have no idea how horrific it is!

44
00:01:50,723 --> 00:01:53,081
That's exactly why I'm curious, Doctor.

45
00:01:53,081 --> 00:01:55,877
If you say something like that one more time, you'd better be ready to get scolded by me, Mr. Hefty!

46
00:01:55,877 --> 00:01:57,510
I told you not to call me that.

47
00:01:57,510 --> 00:02:01,272
I will so long as you're still calling my son a twerp! Isn't that right, my lovely son?

48
00:02:01,272 --> 00:02:02,567
Here's our big boy.

49
00:02:02,567 --> 00:02:05,450
Come on. You're the last Cardbot in Mowtown to be vaccinated.

50
00:02:05,450 --> 00:02:08,388
Hmph! That kind of impurity has no place in my body.

51
00:02:08,388 --> 00:02:11,550
Hey! Vaccines are pointless unless everyone gets vaccinated!

52
00:02:11,550 --> 00:02:13,512
Here. Make sure you do it yourself then.

53
00:02:13,512 --> 00:02:18,054
Hmph! If I take down all the Wild Cardbots that come at me, THAT'S prevention!

54
00:02:18,054 --> 00:02:19,903
He doesn't seem to realize how serious the situation is.

55
00:02:19,903 --> 00:02:21,790
No, that guy just doesn't want to get his shots. 

56
00:02:21,790 --> 00:02:23,567
You're running away because you're a scaredy cat!

57
00:02:23,567 --> 00:02:24,798
You being a big baby!

58
00:02:24,798 --> 00:02:25,780
SHUT UP!

59
00:02:26,545 --> 00:02:28,882
There. I did all I could do for him.

60
00:02:28,882 --> 00:02:30,855
Thank you. Leave the rest to me.

61
00:02:32,724 --> 00:02:33,781
Rear side next.

62
00:02:33,781 --> 00:02:34,441
Okay!

63
00:02:35,164 --> 00:02:37,233
Jun, Crest is here.

64
00:02:37,233 --> 00:02:39,275
Hello, ma'am. How's Blue Cop doing?

65
00:02:39,974 --> 00:02:44,425
These bandages will activate the nanomachines inside your body to help you recover. Make sure to get plenty of rest for now.

66
00:02:44,425 --> 00:02:46,406
That's right, Bluey. Don't push yourself too hard.

67
00:02:46,605 --> 00:02:47,609
Yes, ma'am.

68
00:02:48,461 --> 00:02:49,799
She's here.

69
00:02:49,799 --> 00:02:51,394
Sky Gallop?

70
00:02:51,394 --> 00:02:54,343
Thou look unusually glum. It doth not suit thou, young master Jun.

71
00:02:54,343 --> 00:02:56,390
Thou also appear to be in a dreadful state, Sir Blue.

72
00:02:56,390 --> 00:02:58,026
What's going on? Why are you here?

73
00:02:58,026 --> 00:02:59,155
I called her to pick me up.

74
00:02:59,155 --> 00:02:59,848
Where are you going?

75
00:02:59,848 --> 00:03:03,481
I was entrusted with the task of transporting vaccines to Porcaca, the hometown of my fair lady Pereru.

76
00:03:03,481 --> 00:03:06,162
There are others across the sea who have been waiting for their vaccinations.

77
00:03:06,162 --> 00:03:08,481
I hast been busy as of late thanks to the increase in the number of deliveries, 

78
00:03:08,481 --> 00:03:12,203
yet the Wild Cardbot business is important to me too. I shall gladly help thee.

79
00:03:12,203 --> 00:03:13,317
We're counting on you.

80
00:03:13,317 --> 00:03:14,735
Send our regards to everyone.

81
00:03:14,735 --> 00:03:15,603
I shall.

82
00:03:15,603 --> 00:03:18,870
Ah... I have heard the tidings. Thou met with Solid Horn, did thou not?

83
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:21,569
I desire to help, yet as thou can see, it is difficult at the moment.

84
00:03:21,569 --> 00:03:26,770
And yet, I came across Sir Iron on mine way hither. As we are fellow transporters, we chat from time to time, and he seemed a bit bored of late.

85
00:03:26,770 --> 00:03:29,195
Should thou bid on him, he would prove a valuable ally.

86
00:03:29,195 --> 00:03:32,106
Right then. Shall we depart, Doctor Ambler?

87
00:03:32,721 --> 00:03:37,031
Jun. If Soleil hadn't sealed Blue Cop inside her Metal Breath, his life would've been in danger.

88
00:03:37,031 --> 00:03:37,439
What?

89
00:03:37,439 --> 00:03:39,711
It means Dr. Rhea's instruction was the right move.

90
00:03:39,711 --> 00:03:41,949
...I was being too mean to Soleil.

91
00:03:41,949 --> 00:03:45,353
Don't worry about it. I'll apologize to Soleil on your behalf.

92
00:03:45,353 --> 00:03:47,579
No. I'll do it myself.

93
00:03:47,579 --> 00:03:48,531
Very well.

94
00:03:49,776 --> 00:03:53,445
Freedom sure is nice. It’s a world of difference from Trion Prison.

95
00:03:53,445 --> 00:03:56,966
But... I’m hungry! I can’t run wild like this!

96
00:03:56,966 --> 00:03:59,759
"You should’ve figured out where those guys were hiding, you moron."

97
00:03:59,759 --> 00:04:03,670
"For someone who calls himself the chieftain, you sure lack any forethought. Thanks to you, we’re stuck wandering around aimlessly."

98
00:04:03,670 --> 00:04:06,498
You fools! What, was I supposed to just sit there and tolerate that kind of humiliation!?

99
00:04:06,498 --> 00:04:07,801
"I guess you couldn’t help it."

100
00:04:07,801 --> 00:04:08,962
"It must’ve been hard to bear."

101
00:04:08,962 --> 00:04:13,239
That’s right. If I had stayed quiet, our comrades in the afterlife would’ve laughed at me.

102
00:04:13,239 --> 00:04:14,359
Man, I’m hungry...

103
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,221
Soleil!

104
00:04:17,221 --> 00:04:18,398
Good morning!

105
00:04:18,398 --> 00:04:19,100
Hello.

106
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:20,319
She's friends with the invaders...!

107
00:04:20,319 --> 00:04:22,415
Vance! You shouldn't say something like that...!

108
00:04:22,415 --> 00:04:22,819
What was that?

109
00:04:22,819 --> 00:04:25,601
Ahem, ah, hah. Sorry. I was talking about the headline of this morning's newspaper:

110
00:04:25,601 --> 00:04:28,211
"Wild Cardbots, the Invaders from Outer Space! Local Lake Gets Destroyed!"

111
00:04:28,211 --> 00:04:31,292
You're working with them, right? What happened there?

112
00:04:31,292 --> 00:04:32,441
This article is full of nonsense!

113
00:04:32,441 --> 00:04:35,680
Nonsense? You think my dad wrote that article based on a lie?

114
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:39,485
Blaion said he wants to serve as a bridge between humans and Wild Cardbots!

115
00:04:39,485 --> 00:04:43,519
So what? You know it's true that our town's been suffering a lot of damages lately because of those Wild Cardbots. 

116
00:04:43,519 --> 00:04:44,411
First there was the refinery fire,

117
00:04:44,411 --> 00:04:45,856
then the multi-vehicle rollover accident,

118
00:04:45,856 --> 00:04:47,202
and just the other day our entire school was almost destroyed.

119
00:04:47,202 --> 00:04:48,850
It's making everyone anxious.

120
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:50,079
We... have the situation under control.

121
00:04:50,079 --> 00:04:52,442
Guys, come on. Take a seat. Class is starting soon.

122
00:04:52,442 --> 00:04:54,132
Then prove it.

123
00:04:54,132 --> 00:04:54,992
You asked for it!

124
00:04:54,992 --> 00:04:56,840
- Waah! Guys! Stop it!
- Yeah!

125
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:58,738
Just give Soleil a chance.

126
00:04:58,738 --> 00:04:59,298
Jun!

127
00:04:59,298 --> 00:05:01,785
I'm all the living, breathing proof you need!

128
00:05:01,785 --> 00:05:07,028
Metal Cardbots also have a history of causing some serious trouble, but now they're Earthlings' friendly neighbors.

129
00:05:07,028 --> 00:05:09,533
For example, Vera. You're friends with Fleta Z, aren't you?

130
00:05:09,533 --> 00:05:10,632
That's true...

131
00:05:10,632 --> 00:05:13,201
Didn't you guys play soccer with Tigun and have a great time, too?

132
00:05:13,201 --> 00:05:15,562
- Y-yeah...
- It was fun...

133
00:05:15,562 --> 00:05:18,185
I believe in Wild Cardbots all the same as Metal Cardbots.

134
00:05:22,356 --> 00:05:23,851
Thank you for what you did back there.

135
00:05:23,851 --> 00:05:27,999
That's what I should be saying. Thanks for saving Blue Cop yesterday, I'm really grateful.

136
00:05:27,999 --> 00:05:30,127
I simply followed my mother's instructions.

137
00:05:30,127 --> 00:05:33,534
I see... Sorry for saying such harsh things.

138
00:05:33,534 --> 00:05:35,283
Uh? I don't mind...

139
00:05:35,283 --> 00:05:36,651
You sure you don't mind?

140
00:05:36,651 --> 00:05:37,353
What?

141
00:05:37,353 --> 00:05:39,865
Well, you certainly did seem to mind what he said.

142
00:05:40,893 --> 00:05:44,620
Jun. How can you be so sure you can trust us?

143
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:46,247
It's just... a hunch. 

144
00:05:46,247 --> 00:05:46,983
A hunch?

145
00:05:46,983 --> 00:05:51,259
Although there were some bumps along the way, I was able to become friends with Tigun and Night Griffon. 

146
00:05:51,259 --> 00:05:52,356
And Phantom Hornet too, of course!

147
00:05:52,356 --> 00:05:53,151
Bzzt!

148
00:05:53,351 --> 00:05:55,531
I'd say the same goes for Solid Horn too.

149
00:05:55,531 --> 00:05:57,002
What an absurd boy he is.

150
00:05:57,002 --> 00:05:58,659
Jun has always been unbelievable like that.

151
00:05:58,659 --> 00:06:03,208
We've watched Jun and the Metal Cardbots go through all kinds of hardships and struggles. 

152
00:06:03,208 --> 00:06:05,300
- He's a little bit reckless,
- Oh, right! We should make friends with Tachy too!

153
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:07,021
- but he always makes it work out in the end.
- Uh... Where in the world do I even look for her? 

154
00:06:07,021 --> 00:06:08,199
- Jun.
- Uh... Where in the world do I even look for her? 

155
00:06:08,199 --> 00:06:10,194
Here. I'm giving them back.

156
00:06:10,194 --> 00:06:11,466
Guys!

157
00:06:11,466 --> 00:06:13,319
It's my gratitude for believing in us.

158
00:06:14,019 --> 00:06:15,305
Thank you...

159
00:06:15,305 --> 00:06:18,589
Now! Shall we set up a plan to seal Solid Horn together?

160
00:06:18,589 --> 00:06:22,377
We can't pinpoint his exact location, but I assume he won't be far from where he crashed on Earth.

161
00:06:22,377 --> 00:06:24,345
And his hunger is surely slowing him down.

162
00:06:24,345 --> 00:06:27,036
Then that also means he can't hide for too long.

163
00:06:27,036 --> 00:06:30,252
He must be starving, so he'll pounce on any food that shows up.

164
00:06:30,252 --> 00:06:31,456
Foo... FOOD!

165
00:06:31,456 --> 00:06:35,252
The closer he gets to the city with plenty of food, the sooner he'll show up right before us!

166
00:06:35,252 --> 00:06:38,158
Is there any way to monitor the areas where he's likely to appear?

167
00:06:38,158 --> 00:06:40,112
I shall be your eye in the sky.

168
00:06:40,112 --> 00:06:42,185
You sure you'll be okay after getting stabbed by that horn?

169
00:06:42,185 --> 00:06:44,713
Hm-hm. Whilst I still need a bit more time to recover,

170
00:06:44,713 --> 00:06:46,941
simply flying through the air is no problem at all for me.

171
00:06:46,941 --> 00:06:50,257
The rhinos have shown up. Sending coordinates now.

172
00:06:50,257 --> 00:06:54,050
Good. Let’s spread out so that we can mobilize as soon as we spot him.

173
00:06:54,050 --> 00:06:56,379
I'll be waiting in the sky with Phantom Hornet.

174
00:06:56,379 --> 00:06:57,985
Then Jun and I will be at the center of-

175
00:06:57,985 --> 00:06:59,420
I told you to get some rest.

176
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:01,661
Get in the car. Big bro's gonna take you there.

177
00:07:01,661 --> 00:07:02,963
You're the best, big bro Edd!

178
00:07:02,963 --> 00:07:05,646
However, I am merely a watcher from above.

179
00:07:05,646 --> 00:07:08,685
I need someone who can accurately assess the enemy’s movements first.

180
00:07:08,685 --> 00:07:10,726
Someone stealthy, if possible.

181
00:07:10,726 --> 00:07:13,060
In that case, there’s only one bot for the job!

182
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:13,812
One bot?

183
00:07:13,812 --> 00:07:17,591
This is Shadow X! Moving towards the coordinates immediately. Over! 

184
00:07:17,591 --> 00:07:20,250
Target spotted! He's attacking an oil tanker!

185
00:07:20,348 --> 00:07:22,882
Uagh!! What are these things?!

186
00:07:22,882 --> 00:07:26,288
Jun, they’re not too far from your current location.

187
00:07:26,288 --> 00:07:26,917
Got it!

188
00:07:26,917 --> 00:07:28,802
Alright. Hold on tight!

189
00:07:29,076 --> 00:07:30,612
Let's hurry, Phantom Hornet.

190
00:07:30,612 --> 00:07:32,091
Bzzt!

191
00:07:32,091 --> 00:07:33,106
Let's go, Wild Guardy.

192
00:07:33,106 --> 00:07:33,687
Hm!

193
00:07:33,687 --> 00:07:35,634
It's gonna be difficult to catch him before he combines, right?

194
00:07:35,634 --> 00:07:39,764
It certainly won't be easy. It'll be best for us to spread out and figure out his exact location.

195
00:07:39,764 --> 00:07:42,449
We have to stop him from gaining energy as quickly as possible.

196
00:07:44,994 --> 00:07:46,437
The truck stopped!

197
00:07:51,156 --> 00:07:52,819
H-help me!!

198
00:07:56,346 --> 00:07:57,824
Finally, a meal!

199
00:07:57,824 --> 00:07:59,420
Solid Horn just combined!

200
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:01,415
He's going for the oil! Hurry, hurry!

201
00:08:01,415 --> 00:08:03,415
We'll be there in a sec! Tigun, you ready?

202
00:08:03,415 --> 00:08:04,860
Anytime!

203
00:08:07,872 --> 00:08:09,819
Feels good to be alive!

204
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:11,088
I see him over there!

205
00:08:11,088 --> 00:08:13,463
Sorry to interrupt your dinner, but... Shoot him, Tigun!

206
00:08:13,463 --> 00:08:14,538
GRRR!!

207
00:08:16,430 --> 00:08:18,408
Even if we manage to prevent him from consuming energy,

208
00:08:18,408 --> 00:08:22,185
it may not so easy to stop him from attacking us with his remaining strength.

209
00:08:25,305 --> 00:08:27,831
Don't disturb a rhino while he's eating!

210
00:08:28,346 --> 00:08:29,564
Tigun! Set Up!

211
00:08:29,725 --> 00:08:32,721
There might be a way to separate Solid Horn's combined form.

212
00:08:32,721 --> 00:08:33,638
Is that possible?

213
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:37,006
I sensed that a powerful magnetic force was generated when he combined. 

214
00:08:37,006 --> 00:08:37,639
Magnetic force...?

215
00:08:37,639 --> 00:08:38,845
You know, how magnets work.

216
00:08:38,845 --> 00:08:42,258
I remember what we learned in science class. Magnetic force weakens when heat is applied.

217
00:08:42,258 --> 00:08:44,121
Oh! That means...!

218
00:08:44,121 --> 00:08:46,671
Blaion, you're up now. Please take care of it.

219
00:08:46,671 --> 00:08:47,802
No need for "please".

220
00:08:50,293 --> 00:08:52,581
That's enough of your reckless stampeding!

221
00:08:53,690 --> 00:08:57,893
You came all this way just to interrupt my meal? You should be ashamed of yourself!

222
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:01,392
But that tactic will be useless if he manages to stop us like last time.

223
00:09:01,392 --> 00:09:04,403
Then we need to make sure to grab him and hold him down...

224
00:09:04,403 --> 00:09:05,515
with brute strength, no less!

225
00:09:05,515 --> 00:09:08,834
I’ve always wanted to see your face, Solid Horn!

226
00:09:09,134 --> 00:09:11,203
Huh? The worst uncle ever is here!

227
00:09:11,203 --> 00:09:13,018
Heavy Iron, Set Up!

228
00:09:13,018 --> 00:09:16,216
So you’re Heavy Iron, the outlaw among Metal Cardbots!

229
00:09:18,115 --> 00:09:19,929
How very flattering that you recognize me!

230
00:09:19,929 --> 00:09:24,077
I heard you broke away from your kind and wandered the planet, destroying everything that doesn't suit your tastes!

231
00:09:24,077 --> 00:09:27,326
Why is someone who's even more beastly than us helping some kid?!

232
00:09:27,326 --> 00:09:28,263
Look out, Heavy Iron!!

233
00:09:28,663 --> 00:09:31,496
That's none of your business. It's just that the world has changed! 

234
00:09:31,496 --> 00:09:32,230
Hey, twerp!

235
00:09:32,230 --> 00:09:34,038
Yeah! Iron Cannon!!

236
00:09:36,294 --> 00:09:37,509
Nice shot, Mr. Hefty!

237
00:09:37,509 --> 00:09:38,801
Soleil! Now!

238
00:09:38,801 --> 00:09:40,263
Yes! Blaion!

239
00:09:40,263 --> 00:09:42,490
Omega Heat Flame!!

240
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:48,051
You smell a lot like me, Heavy Iron.

241
00:09:48,051 --> 00:09:52,686
Judging by that expression of utter boredom on your face, I guess you don't like being in this situation either, do you?

242
00:09:52,686 --> 00:09:53,834
Am I right?

243
00:09:58,951 --> 00:10:01,022
Heavy Iron! Please hang in there a little longer!

244
00:10:01,022 --> 00:10:02,764
This doesn't even make me sweat.

245
00:10:04,462 --> 00:10:07,697
Jun said... he believes in the Wild Cardbots. 

246
00:10:07,697 --> 00:10:10,583
Now... It's our turn to live up to that trust!!

247
00:10:11,565 --> 00:10:13,206
Now, you twerps!

248
00:10:13,913 --> 00:10:16,400
Fire Roar Blaze!!

249
00:10:17,245 --> 00:10:21,037
Fire Roar... Blaze!!

250
00:10:32,317 --> 00:10:33,138
You did it!!

251
00:10:33,138 --> 00:10:34,437
Blaion!

252
00:10:34,437 --> 00:10:35,937
I'm so sorry for making you do such a reckless thing.

253
00:10:35,937 --> 00:10:38,894
I'm fine. Just seal him already!

254
00:10:38,894 --> 00:10:40,491
You did a great job, Blaion.

255
00:10:40,719 --> 00:10:43,436
Soleil. Looks like it's your turn.

256
00:10:43,436 --> 00:10:45,389
Ah... Okay. 

257
00:10:45,389 --> 00:10:46,640
Huh?

258
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:47,923
Heavy Iron?

259
00:10:47,923 --> 00:10:49,884
Oi... What do you think you're doing?

260
00:10:49,884 --> 00:10:51,288
A new kind of power, huh...?

261
00:10:51,288 --> 00:10:52,428
No, Heavy Iron!!

262
00:11:00,437 --> 00:11:01,374
Uncle!!

263
00:11:02,758 --> 00:11:03,594
Done!

264
00:11:03,594 --> 00:11:05,130
I think it's a perfect plan.

265
00:11:05,130 --> 00:11:08,259
Of course there are still variables to consider, but for now, this seems like the best option.

266
00:11:08,259 --> 00:11:10,482
Alright! We got ourselves a plan, so let's head out!

267
00:11:10,482 --> 00:11:13,378
Jun. We'd love to go with you, but we know we'll just be a burden.

268
00:11:13,378 --> 00:11:14,826
Please come back safe and sound!

269
00:11:14,826 --> 00:11:17,009
Yep! You can count on it. Let's go!

270
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:20,461
Uh... what are you doing over there, Heavy Iron? We're heading out now.

271
00:11:20,461 --> 00:11:21,822
Something on your mind?

272
00:11:21,822 --> 00:11:24,376
I'm just looking forward to the first real fight I've had in a while.

273
00:11:24,376 --> 00:11:28,057
All you have to do is stop him from going on a rampage, so don't get carried away.

274
00:11:28,057 --> 00:11:29,591
I'll try.

275
00:11:31,506 --> 00:11:32,879
Heavy Iron...!!

